{\plain \fs40 \i\f3\fs40 Concerning the Service}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f3  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 In the course of their Christian development, those baptized at an\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 early age are expected, when they are ready and have been duly prepared,\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 to make a mature public affirmation of their faith and commitment to the\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 responsibilities of their Baptism and to receive the laying on of hands\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 by the bishop.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 Those baptized as adults, unless baptized with laying on of hands by a\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 bishop, are also expected to make a public affirmation of their faith\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 and commitment to the responsibilities of their Baptism in the presence\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 of a bishop and to receive the laying on of hands.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 When there is no Baptism, the rites of Confirmation, Reception, and the\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 Reaffirmation of Baptismal Vows are administered in the following form.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 If desired, the hymn Gloria in excelsis may be sung immediately after\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 the opening versicles and before the salutation {\u8220\'93}The Lord be with you.{\u8221\'94}\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 The Nicene Creed is not used at this service.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 It is appropriate that the oblations of bread and wine be presented by\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f3\fs20 persons newly confirmed.}{\plain \fs24 \f3 \par
